      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17293222_0080.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140424_17293222_0080&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17293222_0080.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17294083_0081.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140424_17294083_0081&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17294083_0081.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;From: Freeda, To: Bess Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Picture Info: 1st M.E. Church, Milford, Illinois, Pub. by C.C.Campbell&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Milford, Illinois on July 24, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bessie Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bess,&lt;br&gt;
Can I walk to school with you this a.m? Gee, I wish I could. Did you get home all O.K.? We 3 girls sure had a circus on our way home. Answer soon.&lt;br&gt;
Freeda&lt;/p&gt;</description>
